   "html_text": "It is possible to see a connection between ideas that are fundamental to interaction theory (which brings together work from phenomenology and embodied cognition) and some ideas that can be found in the work of Stanley Cavell (which aims to interpret and develop the work of Austin and Wittgenstein, as well as integrating work from phenomenology with work in analytic philosophy). Where Gallagher and Zahavi emphasize social interaction, Cavell writes of a duality in the problem of other minds. Cav",
   "md_text": "It is possible to see a connection between ideas that are fundamental to interaction theory (which brings together work from phenomenology and embodied cognition) and some ideas that can be found in the work of Stanley Cavell (which aims to interpret and develop the work of Austin and Wittgenstein, as well as integrating work from phenomenology with work in analytic philosophy). Where Gallagher and Zahavi emphasize social interaction, Cavell writes of a duality in the problem of other minds. Cav"
